  "body": "Stacked on #2927 (merge #2927 first).\n\n## What changed\n\n- The STEP model import expands two more ISO 10303-21 short names: `PLANUN` (`PLANE_ANGLE_UNIT`) and `GC` (`GLOBAL_UNCERTAINTY_ASSIGNED_CONTEXT`).\n- The `GUAC` and `SUNT` names of #2927 move into the same table, in the new module `crates/kernel/src/step_units_guard.rs`.\n- A new check refuses a file by name when a plane angle unit cannot be converted to radians.\n- The check also refuses a unit that measures a plane angle but is not marked as one. An angle is never read in a unit that the file does not state.\n- New fixture `testdata/models/short_units_degree_cone.step`. It is our own 1 degree draft frustum (base radius 10 mm, height 10 mm), with short-name units.\n- The STEP agreement bench gets a `Truck::NotRecorded` variant. #2790 removed the truck reader, so a new fixture has no truck reading. The bench must not make one up.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe pinned p21 parser leaves `PLANUN` short. The solidcore-step unit reader then does not find the plane angle unit and uses radians. The cone semi-angle of 1 degree was read as 1 radian. With our fixture, the pcurve check then refused the solid with a misleading reason: \"an edge lies 8.32 mm off the face's surface\". A file whose edges do not hold the surface could pass with the wrong shape.\n\nThe short names come from the issue's reading of the public ISO short-name registry (`PLANUN` at line 1554). I could not fetch the registry again in this session.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (red before the fix):\n\n- `step_short_units::short_name_degree_cone_keeps_its_angle`: volume and top radius of the 1 degree frustum. Before the fix: refused, \"an edge lies 8.32039972978102 mm off the face's surface\".\n- `step_short_units::unmarked_angle_unit_is_refused_by_name`: the degree unit without its marker is refused, and the message names `#13`. Before the fix: the misleading pcurve refusal.\n- `step_units_guard::tests::short_name_context_reads_degrees_and_uncertainty`: degrees and the `GC` uncertainty are read.\n- `step_units_guard::tests::angle_unit_on_a_steradian_is_refused`.\n\nControls (green before and after): `long_name_degree_cone_control_keeps_its_angle`, `degree_unit_passes_the_angle_check`, and the five #2927 tests.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- M1: remove the `PLANUN` mapping. The cone pin is red, and the check alone refuses the file by name (\"unit #13 measures a plane angle but is not marked...\"). Restored: green.\n- M2: remove the `GC` mapping. The uncertainty unit test is red (`uncertainty: None`). Restored: green.\n- M3: remove the `check_angle_units` call. The refusal pin is red. Restored: green.\n- M4: skip the base-unit check. The steradian unit test is red. Restored: green.\n\nGates on the final code:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base base-2927` (the head of #2927): 82 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"kernel heavy\"`: 16 steps, 0 failed (lib, bins, agreement, blend, heal_import, import_corpus, machining_mesh_shortfalls, mesh_deviation_bench, solidcraft_hostile, solidcraft_import, step_agreement, step_closed_form, step_import, step_short_units, step_twisted_flank, doc).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes of `motion` and `app` were not run. They are reached only through the crate dependency graph (the `lib.rs` change). They must run before this PR is ready.\n- The bench's raw tessellator (test-only `step_util::solidcore_mesh`) does not expand short names. #2919 recorded the same for lengths. Its pinned verdict for the new fixture is its refusal. The app meshes the record from `read_step`, which is correct.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2927 changes the same rename step in `read_guarded` (`crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step.rs`). This PR is stacked on it.\n\nChangelog: STEP import reads a plane angle unit given by its short name (PLANUN), and refuses by name an angle unit that it cannot read, so an angle in degrees is never read as radians.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2973\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
